:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=VOLS SCROLL=YES EXTACT=YES.(No optical volumes)
:LISTACT OPTION=1 ACTFOR=EXTACT ENTER='CMD ?ADDOPTCTG' HELP='WRKOPTVOL/OPTIONS'.1=Add
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 102' HELP='WRKOPTVOL/OPTIONS'.2=Change
:LISTACT OPTION=3 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 103' HELP='WRKOPTVOL/OPTIONS'.3=Copy
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 104' HELP='WRKOPTVOL/OPTIONS'.4=Remove
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DSPOPT VOL(&VOL.) DEV(&DEV.)' HELP='WRKOPTVOL/OPTIONS'.5=Display
:LISTACT OPTION=8 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD WRKLNK OBJ(''/QOPT/&VOL.'')' HELP='WRKOPTVOL/OPTIONS'.8=Work with directories
:LISTACT OPTION=10 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?INZOPT VOL(&VOL.) DEV(&DEV.)' HELP='WRKOPTVOL/OPTIONS'.10=Initialize
:LISTACT OPTION=11 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD WRKLNK OBJ(''/QOPT/&VOL./*'')' HELP='WRKOPTVOL/OPTIONS'.11=Work with object links
:LISTACT OPTION=12 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?DUPOPT FROMVOL(&VOL.) FROMDEV(&DEV.)' HELP='WRKOPTVOL/OPTIONS'.12=Duplicate ...
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKOPTVOL/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=VOL USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=7 EXTACT=YES HELP='FLD/VOL'.Volume
:LISTCOL VAR=DEV USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=21 HELP='FLD/DEV'.Device
:LISTCOL VAR=VOLTYPE USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=33 HELP='FLD/VOLTYPE'.Volume Type
:LISTCOL VAR=MEDTYPE USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=47 HELP='FLD/MEDTYPE'.Media Type
:LISTCOL VAR=AUTL USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=57 HELP='FLD/AUTL'.Authorization List
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=DSPTAP.Display Tape Volume Information - Help
:P.The labels of one file of the volume in the tape device, under the
volume's own. Enter goes on to the next file, F14 back to the one
before; page down for the file's dates and the system that wrote it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPTAPSAV.Display Saved Objects - Help
:P.What one file of the tape holds. For a save, its library and objects;
F11 switches to the objects' texts and F16 shows how and where the save
was made. Enter goes on to the next file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPTAPCTG.Display Tape Cartridge - Help
:P.One cartridge of a media library: its volume, category and where it
is now. Enter shows the next cartridge that matched.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPOPT.Display Optical - Help
:P.An optical volume: its attributes, its directories, its files, or the
objects its save files hold, as DATA asked.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKOPTVOL.Work with Optical Volumes - Help
:P.The optical volumes in the system's optical devices. Type the device
to show only its volumes; 5 shows a volume, 8 its directories.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=KEYSHLP.Function keys - Help
:P.F3 and F12 leave; F5 reads the volumes again.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKIMGCLG.Work with Image Catalogs - Help
:P.Each image catalog is a directory of virtual optical images or virtual
tape volumes. Load one on a virtual device to use its volumes; F11
switches between the status columns and the catalogs' texts.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKIMGCLGE.Work with Image Catalog Entries - Help
:P.The volumes of one catalog. A loaded entry is in the device; the
mounted one is the volume the device presents. Option 1 on the first
line adds an image at the index typed there; F6 loads or unloads the
catalog.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKTAPCTG.Work with Tape Cartridges - Help
:P.The cartridges a media library holds. New ones arrive in *INSERT;
add them to a category before use. Mount moves a cartridge into a drive,
demount sends it back to its slot, remove ejects it to a station.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKMLBSTS.Work with Media Library Status - Help
:P.Each media library and its drives. An allocated drive is held by this
system, an unprotected one is used when needed, a deallocated one never.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/CLGKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F11=View descriptions
:PD.View descriptions.
:PT.F11=View status and devices
:PD.View status and devices.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKIMGCLG/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CLG'.Image Catalog
:P.The image catalog, which holds the image files of a virtual tape or
optical device.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CLGSTS'.Status
:P.The status of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CLGTYPE'.Type
:P.The type of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CLGASP'.ASP Threshold
:P.The ASP Threshold of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CLGDEV'.Device
:P.The device the data goes to.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DEVSTS'.Device Status
:P.The device Status of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKIMGCLG/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Create
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to create it. The Create
Image Catalog (CRTIMGCLG) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it. The Delete
Image Catalog (DLTIMGCLG) command runs for the entry.
:PT.8=Load
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to load it. The Load or
Unload Image Catalog (LODIMGCLG) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.9=Unload
:PD.Type 9 next to an entry and press Enter to unload it. The Load or
Unload Image Catalog (LODIMGCLG) command runs for the entry.
:PT.10=Verify
:PD.Type 10 next to an entry and press Enter to verify it. The Verify
Image Catalog (VFYIMGCLG) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.12=Work with entries
:PD.Type 12 next to an entry and press Enter to work with entries it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKIMGCLG2/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CLGTEXT'.Text
:P.The text of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKIMGCLG2/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Create
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to create it. The Create
Image Catalog (CRTIMGCLG) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it. The Delete
Image Catalog (DLTIMGCLG) command runs for the entry.
:PT.8=Load
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to load it. The Load or
Unload Image Catalog (LODIMGCLG) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.9=Unload
:PD.Type 9 next to an entry and press Enter to unload it. The Load or
Unload Image Catalog (LODIMGCLG) command runs for the entry.
:PT.10=Verify
:PD.Type 10 next to an entry and press Enter to verify it. The Verify
Image Catalog (VFYIMGCLG) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.12=Work with entries
:PD.Type 12 next to an entry and press Enter to work with entries it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/ENTKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F6=Load/Unload image catalog
:PD.Load/Unload image catalog.
:PT.F7=Verify image catalog
:PD.Verify image catalog.
:PT.F8=Reorder by index
:PD.Reorder by index.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F24=More keys
:PD.Shows the other function keys of the display.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CLGDIR'.Directory
:P.The directory shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKIMGCLGE/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/IDX'.Index
:P.The index of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ENTSTS'.Status
:P.The status of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/IMGFILE'.Image File Name
:P.The image File Name of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKIMGCLGE/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Add
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to add it. The Add Image
Catalog Entry (ADDIMGCLGE) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change
Image Catalog Entry (CHGIMGCLGE) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.4=Remove
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to remove it. The Remove
Image Catalog Entry (RMVIMGCLGE) command runs for the entry.
:PT.6=Mount
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to mount it. The Load/Unload
Image Catalog Entry (LODIMGCLGE) command runs for the entry.
:PT.8=Load
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to load it. The Load/Unload
Image Catalog Entry (LODIMGCLGE) command runs for the entry.
:PT.9=Unload
:PD.Type 9 next to an entry and press Enter to unload it. The
Load/Unload Image Catalog Entry (LODIMGCLGE) command runs for the entry.
:PT.10=Initialize volume
:PD.Type 10 next to an entry and press Enter to initialize volume it.
:PT.12=Work with volume
:PD.Type 12 next to an entry and press Enter to work with volume it.
:EPARML.
