:HELP NAME='WRKOPTVOL/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Add
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to add it. The Add Optical
Cartridge (ADDOPTCTG) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it.
:PT.3=Copy
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to copy it.
:PT.4=Remove
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to remove it.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it. The Display
Optical (DSPOPT) command runs for the entry.
:PT.8=Work with directories
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to work with directories it.
The Work with Object Links (WRKLNK) command runs for the entry.
:PT.10=Initialize
:PD.Type 10 next to an entry and press Enter to initialize it. The
Initialize Optical (INZOPT) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.11=Work with object links
:PD.Type 11 next to an entry and press Enter to work with object links
it. The Work with Object Links (WRKLNK) command runs for the entry.
:PT.12=Duplicate ...
:PD.Type 12 next to an entry and press Enter to duplicate &period... it.
The Duplicate Optical (DUPOPT) command is prompted for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
